  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of Animal Sanctuary in Quetta</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Pakistan more than 60,000 dogs die every year on the streets of Pakistan and it is the government itself that orders the mass killing and poisoning of the animals in almost every city of the country. They are shot or poisoned and then their dead bodies are collected by municipal workers, loaded and piled onto trucks for disposal. Quetta, Karachi and Lahore have the highest rate of dog killings each year with over 40,000 dogs killed in these three cities alone. Animals need to be safe.</narrative>
  </description>
